{%- set faqs = [
  ["What are cyber security consulting services?", "Cyber security consulting services help organizations identify security vulnerabilities, assess cyber risks and improve security controls across applications, networks, cloud infrastructure and business systems. These services provide actionable recommendations to reduce security exposure and strengthen data protection."],
  ["Why does a business need cyber security consulting?", "Cyber security consulting helps businesses identify weaknesses before they lead to data breaches, operational disruptions or unauthorized access. It also supports risk-based security planning and helps organizations prioritize investments according to their security needs."],
  ["What services are included in cyber security consulting?", "Common services include cyber risk assessments, security audits, Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT), cloud security reviews, application security assessments, compliance gap analysis and security policy reviews. The scope depends on the organization's requirements and risk exposure."],
  ["How does a cyber security risk assessment work?", "A cyber security risk assessment evaluates critical assets, potential threats, existing vulnerabilities and security controls. The findings are prioritized according to severity and potential business impact to guide risk mitigation and security improvements."],
  ["Which cybersecurity frameworks can consulting services cover?", "Cybersecurity assessments can reference frameworks and standards such as NIST Cybersecurity Framework (NIST CSF), ISO 27001, CIS Benchmarks and SOC 2. The applicable framework depends on business objectives, industry requirements and compliance obligations."],
  ["What deliverables can we expect from a cyber security consulting engagement?", "Typical deliverables include a security assessment report, cyber risk register, compliance gap analysis, remediation recommendations and a prioritized security roadmap. Executive summaries can also help leadership understand key risks and plan security investments."],
  ["How long does a cyber security consulting engagement take?", "The timeline depends on the assessment scope, size of the IT environment, number of systems involved and complexity of the requirements. A focused assessment may take days or weeks, while a broader security program review may require several weeks or longer."],
  ["What is the difference between cyber security consulting and VAPT?", "Cyber security consulting covers broader security strategy, risk management, governance and control improvements. Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) focuses on identifying and validating technical vulnerabilities within a defined scope and can form part of a wider consulting engagement."],
  ["Can cyber security consulting help with compliance requirements?", "Yes. Consulting services can identify gaps between existing security controls and applicable standards or regulations. Recommendations may cover corrective actions, security documentation and compliance readiness, although certification or regulatory compliance cannot be guaranteed through consulting alone."],
  ["Does CipherTrivia provide cloud security consulting?", "Cloud security consulting can cover AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud Platform (GCP). Depending on the engagement scope, reviews may include identity and access management, cloud configurations, network security, storage permissions, logging and data protection."],
  ["When should a business review its cybersecurity strategy?", "A business should review its cybersecurity strategy when adopting new technologies, migrating to the cloud, expanding operations or facing new compliance requirements. Periodic reviews and assessments following security incidents can also help identify emerging risks and improve security controls."],
  ["How can we get started with CipherTrivia's cyber security consulting services?", "Start by discussing your IT environment, security concerns and business objectives with CipherTrivia. The engagement can then be scoped around relevant risk assessments, security control reviews, compliance gaps and prioritized improvement recommendations."]
] %}

